    "problem": "Previous climate models simulating the thermohaline circulation\u2019s response to CO2 were limited by their reliance on unphysical \u2018flux adjustments\u2019 and their inability to accurately model deep-water formation, creating uncertainty in their predictions.",
    "method": "The authors use a coupled ocean-atmosphere general circulation model (HadCM3), without unphysical flux adjustments, to simulate the spatial changes in the North Atlantic thermohaline circulation under different scenarios of increased atmospheric CO\u2082 concentrations.",
    "task": "The task is to simulate the changing spatial structure of the thermohaline circulation in response to atmospheric CO2 forcing using a climate model, in order to identify a potentially observable pattern for monitoring anthropogenic influence on ocean circulation.",
